On mobile devices with system dark mode enabled, Tailwind's default `darkMode: 'media'` strategy auto-applies `dark:` utilities via `prefers-color-scheme`, while the theme toggle only manages `.dark-mode` class for custom CSS, causing half the page to render in dark mode and half in light mode.

## Changes

**header.php**
- Configure Tailwind to use `darkMode: 'class'` before CDN loads
- Apply both `dark` and `dark-mode` classes immediately on page load based on localStorage
- Update `applyTheme()` to manage both classes simultaneously
- Extend all CSS selectors to respond to both `.dark` and `.dark-mode` classes

**footer.php**
- Update theme toggle to call centralized `applyTheme()` function
- Change `updateIcons()` to check `dark` class as source of truth

## Example

```javascript
// Before Tailwind loads
window.tailwind = { config: { darkMode: 'class' } };

// Synchronize both classes
function applyTheme() {
    const isDark = localStorage.getItem('darkMode') === 'true';
    if (isDark) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('dark', 'dark-mode');
        document.body.classList.add('dark', 'dark-mode');
    } else {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark', 'dark-mode');
        document.body.classList.remove('dark', 'dark-mode');
    }
}
```

```css
/* CSS now responds to both classes */
.dark, .dark-mode {
    --bg-page: #121212;
    --text-main: #e5e5e5;
}
```

